-16T22:20:14.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50504530/rivers-says-nc-state-only-college-job-taken","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"David Hale","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Wake Forest up to No. 10 in AP poll as top teams avoid upsets","description":"Wake Forest's move up to No. 10 was the only week-over-week change atop the AP poll as the top nine teams remained unchanged.","published":"2026-11-16T20:48:17.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50504044/wake-forest-no-10-ap-poll-top-teams-avoid-upsets","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Texas' Manning to participate in senior day, mum on future","description":"Texas quarterback Arch Manning said Monday he will participate in Saturday's senior day ceremonies despite having one year of eligibility remaining.","published":"2026-11-16T20:31:37.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50503997/texas-arch-manning-participate-senior-day","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Wisconsin safety Matt Jung to have season-ending ankle surgery","description":"Wisconsin safety Matt Jung will undergo season-ending ankle surgery, the school announced Monday.","published":"2026-11-16T21:10:19.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50503973/wisconsin-safety-matt-jung-season-ending-ankle-surgery","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Texas DL Hero Kanu undergoes season-ending surgery on arm","description":"Texas starting defensive tackle Hero Kanu had season-ending surgery on his arm Monday, coach Steve Sarkisian announced.","published":"2026-11-16T20:55:33.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50503942/texas-dl-hero-kanu-undergoes-season-ending-surgery-arm","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Cignetti: Narrative surrounding Indiana serves as motivation","description":"Indiana coach Curt Cignetti thinks his team's accomplishments continue to be unfairly discredited, and he's using it for motivation as the Hoosiers chase another national title.","published":"2026-11-16T19:38:58.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50503441/narrative-surrounding-indiana-serves-motivation","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4870711/amare-ferrell","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amare_Ferrell"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Amare Ferrell","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amare_Ferrell","description":"American football player (born 2005)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:36:34Z","intro":"Amare Ferrell (born June 14, 2005) is an American college football safety for the Indiana Hoosiers.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Ferrell attended Columbia High School in Lake City, Florida. He was rated as a three-star recruit and committed to play college football for the Indiana Hoosiers over offers from schools such as Cincinnati, Florida State, Louisville, Kentucky, Miami, and Penn State."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"As a freshman in 2023, Ferrell appeared in all 12 games for the Hoosiers, totaling nine tackles. In the 2024 season opener, he recorded his first career interception against FIU. In week 3, Ferrell recorded an interception in the fourth quarter in a 42–13 win over UCLA. In 2025, Ferrell won the National Championship with the Hoosiers against the Miami Hurricanes."}]}}